## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design a compliant, scalable OpenAI integration with policy guardrails in a multi-tenant fintech context, including data lineage and auditability.

## Key Concepts

- Guardrails and policy engine for PII and regulatory compliance
- Per-tenant RBAC via Azure AD and Purview metadata
- Grounding OpenAI outputs to a versioned KB in Blob via Cognitive Search
- Auditing and data lake lineage, retention, and tamper resistance
- Validation plan with synthetic prompts, redaction checks, and leakage tests

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: illustrate policy check flow
function checkPolicy(tenantId, prompt) {
  const policies = loadPolicies(tenantId);
  if (containsPII(prompt) || violatesRegulations(prompt, policies)) {
    redact(prompt);
    throw new Error("Policy violation");
  }
  return prompt;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for prompt injection across tenants in this setup?
- How would you scale the policy engine to support 100s of tenants with individualized rules?

## Why This Is Asked

Data provenance in multi-tenant analytics platforms is critical for compliance, cross-tenant data sharing, and debugging lineage issues. This question evaluates the ability to integrate Azure data cataloging services, OpenAI-powered analysis, and per-tenant security controls into a production-grade pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- Data provenance and lineage tracking
- Microsoft Purview for metadata management
- Cognitive Search-powered versioned knowledge base
- Role-based access control (RBAC) with Azure Active Directory
- Data Lake auditing and logging
- Drift detection in ingestion pipelines

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lineage consistency validation
const validateLineage = (event) => {
  return event.source && event.sink && event.transactionId;
};

// Drift detection logic
const detectDrift = (expected, actual) => {
  return expected.source !== actual.source || 
         expected.sink !== actual.sink;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle real-time vs. batch lineage processing?
- What strategies would you use to minimize AI hallucinations when assessing lineage accuracy?
- How would you design the RBAC model to support nested tenant hierarchies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical Azure OpenAI integration in a glossary domain, emphasizing data residency, compliance, and end-to-end data flow.

## Key Concepts
- APIM-backed OpenAI calls with guided prompts
- Cognitive Search grounding over a versioned KB in Blob
- Text Analytics for PII redaction
- Tenant isolation via Key Vault
- Data Lake audit logging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal pseudo example for OpenAI call with a prompt
async function askGlossary(input, context) {
  const redacted = redactPII(input);
  const results = await cognitiveSearchGround(redacted, context.kb);
  const prompt = `Provide a glossary entry for: ${results.snippet}`;
  return await openai.chatCompletion(prompt, context);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant data residency boundary violations?
- How would you handle updates to the glossary KB versioning and cache invalidation?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests knowledge of Azure OpenAI integration, policy-based gating, and tenant isolation in a practical chat app.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-policy retrieval from Azure Key Vault
- Input screening with Azure Text Analytics
- Policy gating before Azure OpenAI calls
- Grounding with Cognitive Search and KB in Blob
- Per-tenant auditing to Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
async function handle(input, tenantId){
  const policy = await fetchPolicy(tenantId)
  if(!passesPolicy(input, policy)) return cannedReply(policy)
  const grounded = groundKB(input)
  return await openAiQuery(grounded)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test different policy rules per tenant?
- How would you handle policy updates without redeploying services?"

## Why This Is Asked
Understands multi-tenant data separation, policy gates, and regulated data handling in Azure OpenAI stacks.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant RBAC with tenant-scoped keys in Key Vault
- PII redaction and data consent gating
- Grounding via Cognitive Search KB + versioning
- Canary deployment and human handoff
- Auditable logging to Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: redact PII using Azure Text Analytics before prompt submission
async function redactPII(input, client) {
  const res = await client.recognizePII(input, { language: 'en' });
  // replace found PII spans with [REDACTED]
  return performRedaction(input, res);
}
```

